&lt;p&gt;The Finance team ensures Affirm remains financially sound and strategically positioned for growth. Our team manages financial planning, accounting, pricing, vendor management, tax, investor relations, and corporate development. We deliver timely insights, accurate reporting, and careful analysis to support decision-making. From day-to-day financial operations to major investments, we enable sustainable, informed growth by maintaining strong fiscal discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;We are looking for a self-motivated, hardworking, and analytically minded professional to join the Strategic Finance team during a pivotal moment of growth! As Affirm Bank is currently in its formation phase, we are actively building out our foundational team. Reporting to the Bank Head of Strategic Finance, the Bank Strategic Finance Lead will play a key role in the formation and operational build-out of the Bank. You will develop and monitor Bank financial and KPI forecasts, drive strategy, and perform financial analyses throughout the Bank. Your work will help set Bank-level goals, annual budgets, capital stress testing and monitoring, and stakeholder guidance, while building the infrastructure to hold the Bank accountable to achieving its goals. You will have a unique opportunity to work cross-functionally and use quantitative insights to drive better decision-making across the organization. The ideal candidate will not only have superb technical skills but also strong interpersonal skills and the ability to influence cross-functionally and present to all levels of the Bank organization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Develop the end-to-end forecasting and budget process, and design, build, and maintain complex financial models to support strategic planning, scenario analysis, and decision-making&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Drive business outcomes and performance management by developing automated financial analytics dashboards and reporting infrastructure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Analyze, diagnose variances, and report realized financial performance to Bank Executives, the Bank CFO, and other company leaders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Develop capital stress testing, ongoing monitoring, and help establish performance measurements and targets while ensuring analytic rigor in decision-making&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Partner closely with Affirm, Inc. cross-functional teams to integrate financial workflows and join a tight-knit team with outsized impact&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Passion and drive to build robust financial models&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s Degree in Business, Finance, Accounting, or related field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;3+ years of relevant experience in analytical roles (e.g., strategic finance, consulting, data science, or analytics)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Strong working knowledge of financial modeling tools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Excellent proficiency in predictive analytics and forecasting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with fintech, lending, and payments business models preferred&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Proven ability to operate with ownership and influence in a fast-paced, dynamic, and ambiguous work environment with strong critical thinking and problem-solving skills&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base Pay Grade - K&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Equity Grade - USA 6&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range. Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include equity rewards, monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;USA base pay range (CA, WA, NY, NJ, CT) per year: $145,000 - $205,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;USA base pay range (All other US states) per year: $128,000 - $188,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location - Remote U.S.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this position.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first with flexibility built in&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Affirm is proud to be a remote-first company. Most roles can be done from almost anywhere within the country of employment. Some positions may occasionally require in-person work at an Affirm office, and a few are office-based due to the nature of the work. All new hires will be invited to attend an in-person onboarding experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits designed for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our benefits reflect our commitment to care, transparency, and flexibility. Here are a few highlights:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health coverage at no cost: We cover 100% of premiums for employees and their dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spending stipends: Monthly stipends support your tech setup, and the ability to choose health and wellness options that are right for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge: Flexible time off and generous holiday calendars help you rest when you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a piece of what you build: Our employee stock purchase plan (ESPP) lets you buy Affirm stock at a discount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to providing an inclusive interview process, including accommodations for candidates with disabilities. If you need support, we’re happy to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For positions based in San Francisco or Los Angeles: Affirm considers qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By clicking &quot;Submit Application,&quot; you acknowledge that you have read Affirm&#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.affirm.com/global-candidate-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Global Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and consent to the use of your personal information as described.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;","departments":[{"id":4141093003,"name":"Bank Strategy","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4005046003}],"offices":[{"id":4013021003,"name":"Remote US","location":null,"child_ids":[],"parent_id":4025301003}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/affirm/jobs/8202705003","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":6056243003,"location":{"name":"Remote US"},"metadata":[{"id":4128552003,"name":"External Department","value":"Finance","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":28890347003,"name":"PERM Job?","value":false,"value_type":"yes_no"}],"id":8202705003,"updated_at":"2026-11-17T18:45:41-05:00","requisition_id":"JR104647","title":"Affirm Bank Treasury Manager","company_name":"Affirm","first_published":"2026-11-17T18:45:41-05:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Affirm, we exist for the moments that matter—giving people a clear, predictable way to pay over time, with no hidden fees, no surprises, and no tradeoffs on what matters most.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Finance team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance team ensures Affirm remains financially sound and strategically positioned for growth. Our team manages financial planning, accounting, pricing, vendor management, tax, investor relations, and corporate development. We deliver timely insights, accurate reporting, and careful analysis to support decision-making. From day-to-day financial operations to major investments, we enable sustainable, informed growth by maintaining strong fiscal discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;We are looking for a proactive and experienced individual to join as Affirm Bank Treasury Manager. As Affirm Bank is currently in its formation phase, we are actively building out our foundational team. Reporting to the Bank CFO, Bank Treasury is responsible for cash management and operations, funding and liquidity planning, and balance sheet risk management for Affirm Bank. As we continue to scale the Bank and build out the foundational team, the ideal candidate should be able to adapt and thrive in a fast-paced environment with an eagerness to learn and grow.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Support all treasury-related functions with a focus on liquidity and funding risk management, cash management, and periodic funding planning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Develop and execute liquidity risk stress testing models, defining stress scenarios, identifying risk exposures, and calibrating underlying model assumptions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Develop and maintain the Contingency Funding Plan (CFP), lead CFP simulations and testing, and track action plan timelines for liquidity events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Maintain and review Early Warning Indicators (EWIs) and existing risk limits, recommending updates and enhancements to balance sheet risk tolerances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Support The Asset Liability Committee (ALCO) reporting and committee presentations under the Bank CFO, benchmarking liquidity and Interest Rate Risk (IRR) profiles against limits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Support quarterly Interest Rate Risk (IRR) stress tests and semi-annual back-testing results reviews for ALCO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Assist with annual policy and assumption reviews, policy exception documentation, and recordkeeping for Liquidity and IRR policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Guide the enhancement of balance sheet risk management reporting analytics and monitoring for senior leadership, regulators, and internal partners&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Work cross-functionally with Affirm Treasury, Capital Markets, Bank Engineering, Strategic Finance, and the Bank Controller / Record to Report teams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;5+ years of treasury or related financial function experience within banking or financial services&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;BA/BS required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Certified Treasury Professional (CTP) preferred&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Broad range of Treasury specific experience with both market facing and risk management exposure at a financial institution and have familiarity with consumer deposits, working capital line, warehouse facilities and other typical financial funding instruments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Possess strong analytical quantitative capabilities with statistical modeling knowledge and background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Proactive self-starter who is eager to learn with positive attitude&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Pay Grade&lt;/strong&gt; - L&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity Grade&lt;/strong&gt; - USA8&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range. Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include equity rewards, monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;USA base pay range (CA, WA, NY, NJ, CT) per year: $165,000 - $225,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;USA base pay range (all other U.S. states) per year: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;$146,000 - &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;$206,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Employees new to Affirm or promoted into a new role, typically begin in the min to mid range.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this position.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Affirm is proud to be a remote-first company! The majority of our roles are remote and you can work almost anywhere within the country of employment. Affirmers in proximal roles have the flexibility to work remotely, but will occasionally be required to work out of their assigned Affirm office. A limited number of roles remain office-based due to the nature of their job responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re extremely proud to offer competitive benefits that are anchored to our core value of people come first. Some key highlights of our benefits package include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health care coverage - Affirm covers all premiums for all levels of coverage for you and your dependents&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Spending Wallets - generous stipends for spending on Technology, Food, various Lifestyle needs, and family forming expenses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off - competitive vacation and holiday schedules allowing you to take time off to rest and recharge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ESPP - An employee stock purchase plan enabling you to buy shares of Affirm at a discount&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe It’s On Us to provide an inclusive interview experience for all, including people with disabilities. We are happy to provide reasonable accommodations to candidates in need of individualized support during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
