&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Lead, hire, and develop a team of engineers across Python and Kotlin tooling. Set clear expectations, provide regular feedback, and build shared ownership and knowledge across the team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Set the technical strategy and roadmap for getting Affirm’s languages and dependencies current and keeping them current. Translate that direction into achievable quarterly goals, balancing migration risk, developer needs, operational work, and team capacity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Drive runtime and dependency upgrades across a large production codebase. Guide compatibility testing, staged rollouts, and recovery plans with service owners and security partners so teams can adopt supported versions safely.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Evolve shared libraries, dependency management, and build tooling for Python and Kotlin services. Make code easier to build, maintain, and extend through clear package boundaries, versioning, reusable configuration, and automated standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Turn repeated migration work into reliable upgrade workflows and self-service automation. Help engineers discover supported dependencies, understand required changes, and validate upgrades with less manual coordination and fewer disruptive catch-up efforts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Partner with CI/CD, Developer Environments, Test Platform, and service teams to deliver tooling that fits how engineers work. Guide architecture and code reviews, investigate difficult failures, and use developer feedback to improve adoption and usability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Own the reliability and support of the team’s tools and services, including monitoring, on-call, incident response, and documentation. Measure progress through supported-version coverage, dependency age, upgrade lead time, and reduced engineering toil.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;7+ years of software engineering experience, including 2+ years of engineering management or equivalent people leadership. A track record of coaching engineers, supporting career growth, and leading a team through complex delivery.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Strong experience building backend systems or developer infrastructure, with depth in Python or Kotlin/Java. You understand language runtimes, package management, dependency resolution, and build systems, and can guide engineers working across both ecosystems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Experience leading migrations, dependency upgrades, or shared library changes across a large codebase. You understand compatibility, transitive dependencies, testing, and safe rollout practices, and have used automation to make repeated changes easier.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Experience treating internal tools and platforms as products: understanding developer needs, setting priorities, and driving adoption across teams. You can connect technical investments to measurable improvements in productivity, reliability, and maintenance cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;The technical judgment to work closely with senior engineers on architecture, review code, and help debug complex build or runtime failures. You balance immediate delivery with maintainability and reliable operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, with experience aligning distributed teams on ownership, tradeoffs, and delivery plans. You can lead through ambiguity, make decisions with incomplete information, and adjust as you learn.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
