&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Senior Director of Product to lead the Affirm Card and Card Platform—owning both the end-user experience, the business outcomes of every card product, and the underlying platform that powers card issuance, authorization, servicing, and partner integrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a pillar-level leadership role responsible for defining strategy, building a high-performing team, and delivering durable business outcomes across one of Affirm’s most strategic product areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the Card domain end-to-end&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive the multi-year vision for Affirm Card across consumer experience, growth, and economics, inclusive of new card products that complement the one we have in market today.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the US direct to consumer card products (Affirm Cards, and in app virtual cards)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee our Card Platform (authorization, ledgering, servicing, controls) which powers the D2C products both domestically and internationally, along with a number of merchant and partner integrations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate company strategy into a coherent roadmap spanning multiple teams and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and scale a high-performing product organization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and develop a team of PMs and PM leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish product standards, operating cadence, and decision frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a durable org that delivers high-quality outcomes without direct involvement in every decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive business outcomes at scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own GMV, engagement, unit economics, and credit outcomes for the Card domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape investment strategy, tradeoffs, and resource allocation across multiple product areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance and Credit to optimize profitability and risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead platform strategy and execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive platform capabilities that unlock velocity across Affirm (APIs, controls, servicing systems)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with Engineering to make cost vs. value tradeoffs at the system level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the Card Platform scales reliably across use cases, geographies, and partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operate as a cross-functional leader&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align senior stakeholders across Engineering, Design, Credit, Legal, Partnerships, and GTM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with external partners (networks, processors, wallet providers)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the Card domain in executive forums and company planning cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product leadership at scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years in product management, with experience leading multi-team product areas or platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of owning large domains or business lines with meaningful financial impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Org-building capability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing managers and building high-performing PM teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to create systems, processes, and culture that scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic and systems thinker&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate at portfolio-level altitude—connecting product decisions to company strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment across second- and third-order tradeoffs, especially in complex systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform + fintech depth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, cards, fintech, or adjacent infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working on both consumer-facing products and backend platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution and influence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive alignment across senior stakeholders and functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product instincts paired with rigorous, data-driven decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Affirm Card is one of the fastest-growing parts of the business and a key driver of long-term differentiation. This role will shape:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How Affirm shows up every day in consumers’ wallets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How we blend debit, credit, and pay-over-time into one experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The platform foundation that enables future financial products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pay Grade - V&lt;br&gt;Equity Grade - 21&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range.&lt;/strong&gt; Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include equity rewards, monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;USA base pay range (CA, WA, NY, NJ, CT) per year: $340,000 - $375,000&lt;br&gt;USA base pay range (all other U.S. states) per year: $305,000 - $340,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first with flexibility built in&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Affirm is proud to be a remote-first company. Most roles can be done from almost anywhere within the country of employment. Some positions may occasionally require in-person work at an Affirm office, and a few are office-based due to the nature of the work. All new hires will be invited to attend an in-person onboarding experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits designed for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our benefits reflect our commitment to care, transparency, and flexibility. Here are a few highlights:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health coverage at no cost: We cover 100% of premiums for employees and their dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spending stipends: Monthly stipends support your tech setup, and the ability to choose health and wellness options that are right for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge: Flexible time off and generous holiday calendars help you rest when you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a piece of what you build: Our employee stock purchase plan (ESPP) lets you buy Affirm stock at a discount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to providing an inclusive interview process, including accommodations for candidates with disabilities. If you need support, we’re happy to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For positions based in San Francisco or Los Angeles: Affirm considers qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;
