cision.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Purchasing Experience product team owns the ‘face of Affirm’, the core checkout experience for millions of Affirm users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Manager on the Terms and Payments team, you will be responsible for designing both the term and payment selection experiences which drive user clarity and confidence at checkout.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;An ideal candidate is one who has worked extensively on consumer experiences at key moments in the product flow.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly cross-functional role that sits at the intersection of Product, Design, Engineering, Research, and Analytics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Own the core checkout experience where consumers select and review their terms and payments — with a focus on driving conversion, clarity, and confidence at the moment of commitment.&lt;br&gt;• Design and run experiments that improve how consumers understand and choose their terms&lt;br&gt;• Define and ship new UX patterns that change the way checkout looks and feels — using research insights, quantitative signals, and close collaboration with design and analytics to move from discovery to launch.&lt;br&gt;• Partner with Legal and Compliance to understand regulatory requirements and how they affect the user experience.&lt;br&gt;• Work alongside international product partners to expand the terms experience into new markets, adapting for local expectations while keeping the design system coherent.&lt;br&gt;• Develop a deep understanding of user behavior and share those insights broadly — helping the team and stakeholders stay grounded in how consumers actually experience checkout.&lt;br&gt;• Drive an ambitious roadmap — identify the highest-leverage opportunities, align cross-functional partners, and own execution from concept through launch and iteration.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• 5+ years of Product Management experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• A strong sense of taste for user experience — you have opinions about what makes an interaction feel clear, considered, and delightful.&lt;br&gt;• Analytical rigor — you&#39;re comfortable digging into data, interpreting experiment results, and turning qualitative and quantitative inputs into insights and product opportunities.&lt;br&gt;• World-class execution with high agency — you ship reliably, identify what matters without waiting to be told, and hold yourself to a high bar on quality and follow-through.&lt;br&gt;• The ability to work closely with cross-functional teams across product, design, engineering, analytics, and research — building trust and driving alignment without relying on authority.&lt;br&gt;• Strong communication skills — you can deliver results, drive narratives, and explain tradeoffs in a way that brings stakeholders along and creates clarity.&lt;br&gt;• Coachability — you seek out feedback, absorb it without defensiveness, and visibly grow from it.&lt;br&gt;• Bonus points if you&#39;ve worked on checkout, e-commerce, or fintech products in the past.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pay Grade - N&lt;br&gt;Equity Grade - 6&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range&lt;/strong&gt;. Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include equity rewards, monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents.)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;CAN base pay range per year: $153,000 - $213,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This posting is for an existing vacancy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first with flexibility built in&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Affirm is proud to be a remote-first company. Most roles can be done from almost anywhere within the country of employment. Some positions may occasionally require in-person work at an Affirm office, and a few are office-based due to the nature of the work. All new hires will be invited to attend an in-person onboarding experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits designed for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our benefits reflect our commitment to care, transparency, and flexibility. Here are a few highlights:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health coverage at no cost: We cover 100% of premiums for employees and their dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spending stipends: Monthly stipends support your tech setup, and the ability to choose health and wellness options that are right for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge: Flexible time off and generous holiday calendars help you rest when you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a piece of what you build: Our employee stock purchase plan (ESPP) lets you buy Affirm stock at a discount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to providing an inclusive interview process, including accommodations for candidates with disabilities. If you need support, we’re happy to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For positions based in San Francisco or Los Angeles: Affirm considers qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
