&lt;p&gt;This role requires someone who can go deep technically, lead through ambiguity, and translate complex internal architecture into clear partner-facing implementation strategies. You will help define the technical go-to-market model, launch readiness framework, support paths, and long-term operating model for an expanding area of Affirm integrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the technical lead and trusted advisor for strategic partners across Affirm’s card and digital banking ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong external technical relationships and communication channels with partner product, engineering, implementation, and support teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own solution discovery, integration design, partner testing, launch readiness, and ongoing technical support across our partner portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate internal product and engineering architecture into partner documentation, implementation playbooks, test plans, support runbooks, and escalation paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering and Product to identify integration gaps, data quality issues, operational risks, and partner-specific requirements before they become launch blockers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Socialize solution designs, tradeoffs, and launch plans across internal and external stakeholders, building consensus across Product, Engineering, Commercial, Legal, Operations, and partner teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical triage for partner issues, including API behavior, latency, error rates, data mismatches, incident management, RCA follow-up, and partner communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish technical operating rhythms for new partner categories, including external architecture reviews, readiness reviews, incident response, and technical health checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We Look For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years in Partner Solutions Engineering, Solutions Architecture, Partner Engineering, customer-facing Software Engineering, or a similar technical role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing launch readiness, partner certification, UAT, incident management, observability, and support models for external integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting complex external integrations across card, payments, or banking platform environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of card and payments systems, including how transaction state, money movement, reconciliation, and partner data flows operate across multi-party financial systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of REST APIs, webhooks, JSON, SDKs, authentication, observability, and secure integration design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read code, inspect logs, debug API behavior, write scripts, and collaborate credibly with software engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Experience leading cross-functional technical programs by managing dependencies, assessing program health, communicating risks to leadership, and holding internal and external teams accountable to launch milestones.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ability to build durable cross-functional and cross-domain relationships across engineering, product, business, and partner teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;Ability to design scalable integration patterns that solve partner needs without creating partner-specific technical debt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base Pay Grade - N&lt;br&gt;Equity Grade - 5&lt;br&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range. Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents). In addition, the employees may be eligible for equity rewards offered by Affirm Holdings, Inc. (parent company).&lt;br&gt;CAN base pay range per year: $153,000 - $213,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This remote role is open only to candidates residing in Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland and Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, or Saskatchewan.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this position.&lt;br&gt;LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first with flexibility built in&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Affirm is proud to be a remote-first company. Most roles can be done from almost anywhere within the country of employment. Some positions may occasionally require in-person work at an Affirm office, and a few are office-based due to the nature of the work. All new hires will be invited to attend an in-person onboarding experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits designed for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our benefits reflect our commitment to care, transparency, and flexibility. Here are a few highlights:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health coverage at no cost: We cover 100% of premiums for employees and their dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spending stipends: Monthly stipends support your tech setup, and the ability to choose health and wellness options that are right for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge: Flexible time off and generous holiday calendars help you rest when you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a piece of what you build: Our employee stock purchase plan (ESPP) lets you buy Affirm stock at a discount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to providing an inclusive interview process, including accommodations for candidates with disabilities. If you need support, we’re happy to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For positions based in San Francisco or Los Angeles: Affirm considers qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;
